# Words kept out of Naughty mode: slurs against people for their race, ethnicity, nationality,
# religion, sexuality, gender identity or disability. One SHA-256 hash (hex) of each lowercase
# word per line, so the slurs are never in the repository as readable text. This keeps them off
# the page; it is not a secret (short words are easy to recover from a hash).
#
# `npm run check:naughty` (and so `npm run build`) fails if a naughty word or clue is one of
# these, a form of one (plural, -ed, -ing, ...), or a compound starting or ending with one.
#
# To add a word: printf '%s' word | sha256sum   (lowercase, no newline), then add the hash.
